---
description: |
  Normalizes a TruePattern rule, a STIX 2.1 Indicator, to OCSF 1.9 OSINT
  Inventory Info.

  The rule text lands in `osint.detection_pattern` and its language in
  `osint.detection_pattern_type`. On top of the generic STIX mapping, the
  operator adds the upstream rule location as `osint.src_url` and the rule as
  an analytic in `osint.related_analytics`, with the rule name and, for Sigma
  rules, the Sigma rule ID as `uid`. The license remains in
  `unmapped.external_references` under the source name `rule-vendor-license`.
  The complete supplied rule text and external references, including notices,
  are preserved. This mapping does not filter rules based on license metadata
  or determine permission to use them.
---

stix::ocsf::normalize
metadata.product = {
  name: "TruePattern",
  vendor_name: "TruePattern",
}
osint = osint.map(rule => {
  ...rule,
  related_analytics: [{
    name: unmapped.name?,
    type: "Rule",
    type_id: 1,
    // Sigma detection findings carry this ID in `finding_info.analytic.uid`.
    uid: rule.detection_pattern.parse_yaml().id? if rule.detection_pattern_type == "sigma",
  }],
  src_url: unmapped.external_references?.where(ref => ref.source_name == "rule-source").first().url?,
  vendor_name: "TruePattern",
})
drop unmapped.name
